-- | The name a generated closure binds for its `index`-th parameter, counting
-- | from zero: `__rdx_1`, `__rdx_2`, ….
-- |
-- | Doc 18 §4's own table spells the first one, and `__rdx_` is the prefix doc
-- | 02 reserves for generated identifiers, so a closure written here can never
-- | capture or shadow a name the author wrote.
-- |
-- | A generator rather than the single constant this replaces, because plan 56
-- | §11.2 needs more than one: a one-of-three partial application binds the two
-- | parameters still missing, and `SECTION_PARAM` could only ever name one.
-- |
-- | **`__rdx_N` and not `__rdx_aN`.** The second family is taken — the clause
-- | lowering's positional binders use it (`signature_from.rs`), so `|__rdx_a1|`
-- | would shadow `fn fib(__rdx_a0: u64)`.
export(crate) closure_param : usize -> String
closure_param index = format! \-> "__rdx_#{index + 1}"
